      "problem": "A book has a mass of $1\\,\\text{lb}.$ What is this mass in ounces?",
      "worked_solution": "A table showing the customary units of mass is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Ton | $\\text{ton}$ | $1\\,\\text{ton}=2,000\\,\\text{lb}$ |\n| Pound | $\\text{lb}$ | $1\\,\\text{lb}=16\\,\\text{oz}$ |\n| Ounce | $\\text{oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\text{lb}$ is equivalent to $16\\,\\text{oz}.$",
